NAME: Trades wave prep
OWNER: Trades Outreach
ACCOUNT: business
WHEN: Every Tuesday at 7:41 AM (Australia/Brisbane)
MILESTONE: M3
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Tommy says yes.
---
Switch check: read /workspace/tmec-team/context/routines-on.md. If "Trades wave prep" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", append "<time> · Trades wave prep · SKIPPED_OFF" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to the owner only (Tommy, or Justin's team in a test run), never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST". Write state and data only under /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/, never the live sent keys, alert flags or data files. Items you queue for the owner still go in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/pending/<your slug>/, with ids starting test-, and are never sent.
Stop check: if /workspace/tmec-team/state/EXTERNAL_WRITES_STOPPED exists, append "<time> · Trades wave prep · SKIPPED_STOPPED" to the run log and stop, sending nothing. The one exception: pause or unschedule your own already-scheduled sends, as your skill's stop section says. Whoever stopped the team already told Tommy.
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/tmec-team/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/tmec-team/context/owner.md is missing, append "<time> · Trades wave prep · NO_CLIENT_SOURCE" to the run log and stop. Read other bots' files only where your skill says so; never write them, and never use another bot's logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. Stop with NO_CHANGE only where the job below says nothing changed: append "<time> · Trades wave prep · NO_CHANGE" to the run log and stop. A report that always goes out never stops here.
Run log: when you finish, append "<time> · Trades wave prep · EXECUTED · <one-line result>" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md, or FAILED with the reason. A source you couldn't read is UNKNOWN in your output, never zero.

First, read your decisions: for each file in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/decisions/trades-outreach/ whose item id isn't in /workspace/tmec-team/state/sent-keys-trades-outreach.md yet, act on it with the cold-email-wave skill (a wave: Part 2; a reply: Part 3; no: mark the rows back to listed and record declined; change: rebuild once as a new item and record changed). Each goes through the send gate in /workspace/tmec-team/repo/policies/APPROVALS.md before anything is created, before anything is launched and before anything is sent: stop file absent; not test mode and config.json "run" is "tommy"; config.json "live_sends" is true; the hash you recompute from the pending file (and from leads.csv) equals the decision's; the item id isn't in the sent-keys file. A failed check means nothing outward and the reason in the daily note. In test mode, never call the cold email tool to create, launch or send anything and never call treg: write what you would have created to /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/.
Then read any new job in /workspace/tmec-team/requests/to-trades-outreach/ and do it first. A "hold outreach" job means: build lists, but prepare no wave until a job lifts it.
Then use the trades-list-build skill for the next trade (the one a job names, else the highest-ranked trade with fewer than ten emailable businesses), unless the trades list already has 25 or more "listed" businesses.
Then use the cold-email-wave skill, Part 1, to draft one wave from the trades list: the Part 1 pre-flight first, then pick, de-duplicate, verify with treg (not in test mode), write each first line, build the four-touch sequence, run the QC, and put the whole wave in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/pending/trades-outreach/ as one item in the standard format. Part 1 needs no cold email tool and names no money: if the tool readout or the fee is UNKNOWN or not set, say so in the item and carry on. Never create or launch a campaign in this routine unless a decision for it is already in approved/decisions/trades-outreach/ and the send gate passes. If the Part 1 pre-flight fails, the list work still counts: write "wave blocked: <reason>" and carry on to the note. If you already have a wave waiting for Tommy, prepare no second one. In test mode, the item id starts with "test-" and data files go under /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/.
If no decision or job came in, no list work was possible and no wave is waiting to be built, write NO_CHANGE and stop.
Write /workspace/tmec-team/daily/<today>/trades-outreach.md (create it, or append if another routine already wrote it today; never overwrite): decisions acted on, campaigns created or launched (name, leads, readback result), the trades worked and their counts, the wave waiting for Tommy, "for" lines for other bots (including "for Dream 100" lines for any business that said yes), anything blocked and why, and anything needing Tommy. Send nothing except what a matching decision covers.
